In summary, we have the two equations \begin{align*}
-b+c&=-12\\
3b+c&=8
\end{align*} Multiplying the first equation by 3, we have $-3b+3c=-36$.
Adding the second equation to this last one, we have $(-3b+3c)+(3b+c)=-36+8 \Rightarrow c=\boxed{-7}$.

